'' --diagnostics-file: a failed LINK is a location-less error (TKO0116), and the run
'' still exits 5, the toolchain's code.
''
'' 'tiko: link failed' was a bare stderr line, so an editor showed a build that never
'' produced an executable as one with no errors. The linker's own lines ('undefined
'' symbol ...') stay on the console, where the editor's log shows them.
''
'' Needs clang and lld, as every test that links does. The symbol is defined nowhere, so
'' the link fails whatever runtime the machine has.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 -o build/.diagfile-link.exe --diagnostics-file build/.diagfile-link.tsv tests/driver/src/diagfile-link.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 5
'' EXPECT-OUT: error TKO0116: link failed (exit
'' EXPECT-FILE-HAS: build/.diagfile-link.tsv :: tiko-diagnostics\t1\nerror\tTKO0116\t\t0\t0\t0\t0\tlink failed (exit
'' EXPECT-FILE-HAS: build/.diagfile-link.tsv :: \nend\t1\t0\t5\n
'' EXPECT-NO-FILE: build/.diagfile-link.exe
